## Peripheral & Protocol Patterns

Glob-triggered safety for drivers and protocols. Recipes: `.cursor/skills/sc-firmware/references/peripherals.md`.

### Must

- Use BSP pin defines (never hardcode raw port/pin in app/driver call sites)
- CRC-check frames before processing; bound payload size; reset parser on inter-byte timeout
- SPI: correct mode from datasheet; keep CS low for full burst; prefer hardware NSS or BSRR for CS
- I2C: external pull-ups on SCL/SDA; per-device timeout; handle NACK/busy with backoff
- DMA: circular mode for continuous streams
- Radio/UHF: wait GDO / IRQ for packet ready; preamble + CRC; bounded retries with backoff
- On LTDC / DMA2D / Cortex-M7 targets: double-buffer LCD; swap on vblank; DMA2D for fill/blit/blend (not CPU pixel loops); framebuffer write-through SDRAM (MPU) or `cache_clean()` before LTDC reload; flush/invalidate D-cache around DMA

### Must not

- Busy-wait on GPIO (`while (button) {}`) - use timer IRQ or RTOS delay
- Bit-bang SPI when the hardware peripheral is available
- Run I2C transactions or full protocol parse inside ISR (ISR may only enqueue bytes / pulse widths)
- Process UART/protocol frames in ISR - dispatch from task context
- Poll radio status registers in a tight loop when a GDO/IRQ pin exists
- Stop/restart circular DMA mid-stream without a defined re-init path
- Use QSPI for frequently-updated wear-sensitive data in production (read-only assets / update path only)
